# Fos Icons

Fos Icons is an MIT icon library: about 1,600 icons in four styles (Regular,
Filled, Duocolor, Duotone) on a 24px grid. Save this file as
`.cursor/rules/fos-icons.mdc`. For live icon search, also add the MCP server
`https://www.fosicons.com/mcp` (https://www.fosicons.com/ai-agents).

## Rules

1. **Never guess an icon name.** Confirm every name with the Fos Icons MCP tools
   (`search_icons`, `check_icon_names`) when they're connected. Otherwise look it
   up in `node_modules/@fos-icons/react/dist/types/index.d.ts`, or check that
   `https://www.fosicons.com/icons/<name>` exists.
2. **Never draw or edit SVG paths.** Use the package component. If no icon
   fits, say so.
3. **Keep the project's icon library.** Only switch to Fos Icons when the user
   asks, or when the project has no icon library.

## Names

Component = icon name in PascalCase + style suffix:

- `fuel-pump` → `FuelPumpRegular`, `FuelPumpFilled`, `FuelPumpDuocolor`, `FuelPumpDuotone`
- Flutter: `FosIcons.fuelPumpRegular`
- The website calls Filled "Solid"; in code it is always `Filled`.

## Packages

- React: `npm install @fos-icons/react`, then `import { CameraRegular } from '@fos-icons/react'`
- Vue 3: `npm install @fos-icons/vue`, same names
- Svelte, SolidJS, Angular, and Flutter aren't on a registry yet; see
  https://www.fosicons.com/docs for setup, and tell the user before installing.

## Usage

- `size` sets width and height (default 24). Use 16 or 20 in dense UI.
- Regular and Filled inherit `currentColor`; set color on the parent.
- Duocolor and Duotone take `primaryColor` and `secondaryColor`; use them for
  large, illustrative spots, not toolbars.
- One style per UI. Regular by default, Filled for a selected or active state.

## Accessibility

- Icons are `aria-hidden` by default. Leave them decorative next to a text label.
- Icon-only button: put `aria-label` on the button, not the icon.
- A standalone icon that carries meaning: pass `title` (`semanticLabel` in Flutter).
